      "content": "Yes, those are exactly the correct values for $Q_1$ and $Q_3$! You have successfully identified all five numbers needed for your diagram.\n\n**Final Answer:**\n- Min: 5\n- $Q_1$: 11,5\n- Median: 25\n- $Q_3$: 33,5\n- Max: 75\n\n---\n### 📖 Formula Breakdown (How It Works):\n* **The Formula:** The five-number summary uses the median position formula $P = \\frac{n+1}{2}$.\n* **What the letters mean:**\n  * $Q_1$ (Lower Quartile): The median of the bottom half of the data.\n  * $Q_3$ (Upper Quartile): The median of the top half of the data.\n* **Why we use it:** This summary helps us see the 'spread' of the data. The box represents the middle 50% of your data, while the whiskers show the range of the outer values.\n\n🎯 **Exam Tip:** Always draw your box and whisker plot on the provided number line using a ruler. In the DBE exam, you get marks for the correct placement of the five points and for drawing the box and whiskers accurately according to your calculated values!"
